-- The course's running counter in the SMV language (NuSMV / nuXmv).
--
-- Same machine as every other file in this folder, written the way a model
-- checker wants it. Compare it to the Z3 encodings: ASSIGN init/next IS the
-- transition relation, just with a syntax that names the variable once instead
-- of writing x and x' side by side.
--
-- Run it in the browser, no install:  https://bit.ly/fmaiv_smvis
-- Or locally:                         NuSMV counter.smv

MODULE main
  VAR
    x : 0..25;                 -- the counter. Bounded here because an explicit
                               -- model checker must enumerate; Z3 let us leave
                               -- it over all of Int.

  ASSIGN
    init(x) := 0;
    next(x) := case
                 x < 10 : x + 1;   -- the guard
                 TRUE   : 0;       -- the reset
               esac;

  -- The safety property. A model checker proves this for EVERY run, with no
  -- bound -- which is the thing bounded model checking could not give us.
  SPEC AG (x <= 10)

  -- True as well, and the interesting one: the machine really does get there.
  SPEC EF (x = 10)

  -- FALSE on purpose. Ask for it and NuSMV hands back a counterexample trace,
  -- which is the same object Z3 gave us as a model.
  SPEC AG (x <= 9)
